# Rust build output. Cargo.lock stays committed: sqlh is a binary, so builds must be reproducible.
/target/

# rustfmt backups; coverage and mutation-testing output
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
mutants.out*/

# MSVC debug symbols and incremental-link files built outside target/
*.pdb
*.ilk

# Executables are never committed (AGENTS.md); releases are GitHub release assets.
*.exe
*.dll

# Secrets, as a safety net: signing happens in Azure (plan-history.md 3.6) and passwords
# live in Credential Manager, so none of these belongs here. Cargo's registry token, if
# CARGO_HOME is ever pointed at the checkout.
.env
.env.*
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
.cargo/credentials
.cargo/credentials.toml

# Logs of local runs and tests can hold server data; keep them in artifacts/.
*.log

# sqlh's own temporary output files (`-o` writes <path>.<pid>-<n>.partial, then renames).
*.partial

# Merge and patch leftovers
*.orig
*.rej

# sqlh connection profiles: they normally live in %APPDATA%, but SQLH_CONFIG can point
# anywhere. They hold server names and logins (never passwords), so keep them out of git.
profiles.toml
profiles.toml.lock
profiles.toml.*.partial

# Disposable experiments and local query results; these may contain real server data.
# Durable examples and test fixtures belong in docs/ or tests/, with synthetic data.
/scratch/
/artifacts/
# Release workflow output (plan-history.md 3.6), if it is run locally.
/dist/
/unsigned/
/build/
/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.html

# Local-only material that is never pushed: the external code reviews (archive/reviews/).
/archive/

# Worktrees that Claude Code and its workflows create inside the checkout.
.claude/worktrees/

# Editors and IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
*.swp
*~

# Personal Claude Code settings and notes (shared settings in .claude/settings.json and the
# shared CLAUDE.md stay tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# MCP client configuration and state, if a client is pointed at the checkout (the interop
# runs of plan-history.md 5.5 kept theirs in scratch/ and outside the repository). Each
# names a profile and a server command, or holds a client's own state, so none belongs
# here: Claude Code's project scope (`claude mcp add -s project` writes .mcp.json),
# OpenCode's project config and folder, and the MCP Inspector's catalog and storage.
/.mcp.json
/opencode.json
/opencode.jsonc
.opencode/
.mcp-inspector/

# Node tooling for those clients: sqlh has no Node code, so an npm install for a test tool
# (the MCP Inspector, 5.5) belongs in scratch/, and what one leaves here is never source.
node_modules/
.npm/
.npm-cache/
/package.json
/package-lock.json

# Codex runtime state if CODEX_HOME is placed inside the checkout.
# Keep AGENTS.md, .agents/skills/, and shared .codex/config.toml, rules and hooks trackable.
.codex/auth.json
.codex/history.jsonl
.codex/sessions/
.codex/archived_sessions/
.codex/log/
.codex/shell_snapshots/
.codex/tmp/
.codex/*.sqlite*
.codex/plugins/cache/
# An explicitly separate, repository-local Codex home is entirely machine-local.
/.codex-home/

# OS clutter
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
